{"id":"092fd487a086bb56ff6679110531e0f17af4fd2b","axis":"silent","repo":"envoyproxy/envoy","sha":"092fd487a086bb56ff6679110531e0f17af4fd2b","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"changelogs/current/minor_behavior_changes/http__body-size-limit-skip-upgrades.rst","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@","+The :ref:`body size limit filter <config_http_filters_body_size_limit>` no longer counts bytes sent","+after the upstream accepts an upgrade such as WebSocket, or a CONNECT request. Those bytes are","+tunneled traffic rather than a request body, and counting them reset long-lived WebSocket","+connections once their total traffic passed the limit. Bytes sent before the upstream accepts are","+still counted, and so are raw TCP tunneled over POST on an ``allow_post`` route and CONNECT-UDP","+that Envoy terminates itself."],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/root/configuration/http/http_filters/body_size_limit_filter.rst","lines":["@@ -9,6 +9,16 @@ with an error code of 413."," * This filter should be configured with the type URL ``type.googleapis.com/envoy.extensions.filters.http.body_size_limit.v3.BodySizeLimit``."," * :ref:`v3 API reference <envoy_v3_api_msg_extensions.filters.http.body_size_limit.v3.BodySizeLimit>`"," ","+For CONNECT requests, and for upgrade requests of any type such as WebSocket, the filter stops","+counting once the upstream accepts the CONNECT or upgrade. Bytes sent after that are tunneled","+traffic rather than a request body. Bytes sent before it, and the ``Content-Length`` check, still","+apply. The filter decides from the request headers the router forwards, so a later filter that","+removes the upgrade headers keeps the body limited. Two kinds of tunnel are answered without an","+upgrade and are still counted, so disable the filter on their routes: raw TCP tunneled over POST on","+a route with :ref:`allow_post","+<envoy_v3_api_field_config.route.v3.RouteAction.UpgradeConfig.ConnectConfig.allow_post>`, and","+CONNECT-UDP that Envoy terminates itself.","+"," Route-Based Filter Control"," --------------------------"," "],"additions":10,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/filters/http/body_size_limit/BUILD","lines":["@@ -20,6 +20,9 @@ envoy_cc_library(","         \"//envoy/http:codes_interface\",","         \"//envoy/http:filter_interface\",","         \"//envoy/stats:stats_macros\",","+        \"//source/common/common:enum_to_int\",","+        \"//source/common/http:header_utility_lib\",","+        \"//source/common/http:utility_lib\",","         \"//source/extensions/filters/http/common:pass_through_filter_lib\",","         \"@envoy_api//envoy/extensions/filters/http/body_size_limit/v3:pkg_cc_proto\",","     ],"],"additions":3,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/filters/http/body_size_limit/body_size_limit_filter.cc","lines":["@@ -3,7 +3,10 @@"," #include \"envoy/extensions/filters/http/body_size_limit/v3/body_size_limit.pb.h\""," #include \"envoy/http/codes.h\""," ","+#include \"source/common/common/enum_to_int.h\""," #include \"source/common/common/logger.h\"","+#include \"source/common/http/header_utility.h\"","+#include \"source/common/http/utility.h\""," "," namespace Envoy {"," namespace Extensions {","@@ -48,7 +51,7 @@ Http::FilterHeadersStatus BodySizeLimitFilter::decodeHeaders(Http::RequestHeader"," }"," "," Http::FilterDataStatus BodySizeLimitFilter::decodeData(Buffer::Instance& data, bool) {","-  if (config_->maxRequestBytes() == 0) {","+  if (tunnel_established_ || config_->maxRequestBytes() == 0) {","     return Http::FilterDataStatus::Continue;","   }"," ","@@ -62,6 +65,35 @@ Http::FilterDataStatus BodySizeLimitFilter::decodeData(Buffer::Instance& data, b","   return Http::FilterDataStatus::Continue;"," }"," ","+Http::FilterHeadersStatus BodySizeLimitFilter::encodeHeaders(Http::ResponseHeaderMap& headers,","+                                                             bool) {","+  if (tunnel_established_ || config_->maxRequestBytes() == 0) {","+    return Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue;","+  }","+  // Read the request headers the router forwarded rather than the ones this filter saw, so a","+  // later filter that strips the upgrade headers also keeps the body limited.","+  const auto request_headers = decoder_callbacks_->requestHeaders();","+  // A malformed HTTP/1 request gets its error reply through this filter before any request headers","+  // exist.","+  if (!request_headers.has_value()) {","+    return Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue;","+  }","+","+  // Stop counting only once the upstream accepts: a CONNECT answered with a 200, or an upgrade","+  // answered with a 101 that carries upgrade headers. The connection manager also treats a failed","+  // handshake that keeps the upgrade headers as a tunnel, but nothing was tunneled, since the","+  // router doesn't send the body upstream until the upstream accepts. So the body stays limited.","+  // The codecs turn an HTTP/2 or HTTP/3 upstream's 200 into a 101.","+  const bool connect_accepted =","+      Http::HeaderUtility::isConnectResponse(request_headers.ptr(), headers);","+  const bool upgrade_accepted =","+      Http::Utility::isUpgrade(*request_headers) &&","+      Http::Utility::getResponseStatus(headers) == enumToInt(Http::Code::SwitchingProtocols) &&","+      Http::Utility::isUpgrade(headers);","+  tunnel_established_ = connect_accepted || upgrade_accepted;","+  return Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue;","+}","+"," void BodySizeLimitFilter::sizeExceeded(uint64_t length, const char* log_message,","                                        const char* reply_text) {","   // A rejection is client-controlled, so it is logged per stream at debug rather than at error:"],"additions":33,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/filters/http/body_size_limit/body_size_limit_filter.h","lines":["@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@ using BodySizeLimitFilterConfigSharedPtr = std::shared_ptr<BodySizeLimitFilterCo","  * A streaming filter that rejects requests exceeding a configured body size limit","  * without buffering the request body.","  */","-class BodySizeLimitFilter : public Http::PassThroughDecoderFilter,","+class BodySizeLimitFilter : public Http::PassThroughFilter,","                             public Logger::Loggable<Logger::Id::http> {"," public:","   BodySizeLimitFilter(BodySizeLimitFilterConfigSharedPtr config);","@@ -62,11 +62,17 @@ class BodySizeLimitFilter : public Http::PassThroughDecoderFilter,","                                           bool end_stream) override;","   Http::FilterDataStatus decodeData(Buffer::Instance& data, bool end_stream) override;"," ","+  // Http::StreamEncoderFilter","+  Http::FilterHeadersStatus encodeHeaders(Http::ResponseHeaderMap& headers,","+                                          bool end_stream) override;","+"," private:","   void sizeExceeded(uint64_t length, const char* log_message, const char* reply_text);"," ","   BodySizeLimitFilterConfigSharedPtr config_;","   uint64_t bytes_received_{};","+  // Set once the upstream accepts an upgrade or CONNECT. Later bytes are not counted.","+  bool tunnel_established_{false};"," };"," "," } // namespace BodySizeLimitFilter"],"additions":7,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/filters/http/body_size_limit/config.cc","lines":["@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ Http::FilterFactoryCb createFilterFactory(","   auto filter_config =","       std::make_shared<BodySizeLimitFilterConfig>(proto_config, scope, stats_prefix);","   return [filter_config](Http::FilterChainFactoryCallbacks& callbacks) -> void {","-    callbacks.addStreamDecoderFilter(std::make_shared<BodySizeLimitFilter>(filter_config));","+    callbacks.addStreamFilter(std::make_shared<BodySizeLimitFilter>(filter_config));","   };"," }"," } // namespace"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"test/extensions/filters/http/body_size_limit/BUILD","lines":["@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@ envoy_extension_cc_test(","         \"//source/extensions/filters/http/body_size_limit:config\",","         \"//source/extensions/filters/http/filter_chain:config\",","         \"//test/integration:http_protocol_integration_lib\",","+        \"@envoy_api//envoy/config/bootstrap/v3:pkg_cc_proto\",","         \"@envoy_api//envoy/config/route/v3:pkg_cc_proto\",","         \"@envoy_api//envoy/extensions/filters/http/body_size_limit/v3:pkg_cc_proto\",","         \"@envoy_api//envoy/extensions/filters/http/filter_chain/v3:pkg_cc_proto\","],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"test/extensions/filters/http/body_size_limit/body_size_limit_filter_integration_test.cc","lines":["@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@","+#include \"envoy/config/bootstrap/v3/bootstrap.pb.h\""," #include \"envoy/config/route/v3/route_components.pb.h\""," #include \"envoy/extensions/filters/http/body_size_limit/v3/body_size_limit.pb.h\""," #include \"envoy/extensions/filters/http/filter_chain/v3/filter_chain.pb.h\"","@@ -10,6 +11,36 @@ namespace {"," "," using BodySizeLimitIntegrationTest = UpstreamDownstreamIntegrationTest;"," ","+// WebSocket over HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 uses extended CONNECT, which is off by default on both sides.","+void allowExtendedConnect(ConfigHelper& config_helper, Http::CodecType downstream,","+                          Http::CodecType upstream) {","+  if (upstream != Http::CodecType::HTTP1) {","+    config_helper.addConfigModifier([upstream](envoy::config::bootstrap::v3::Bootstrap& bootstrap) {","+      ConfigHelper::HttpProtocolOptions protocol_options;","+      auto* http_config = protocol_options.mutable_explicit_http_config();","+      if (upstream == Http::CodecType::HTTP2) {","+        http_config->mutable_http2_protocol_options()->set_allow_connect(true);","+      } else {","+        http_config->mutable_http3_protocol_options()->set_allow_extended_connect(true);","+      }","+      ConfigHelper::setProtocolOptions(*bootstrap.mutable_static_resources()->mutable_clusters(0),","+                                       protocol_options);","+    });","+  }","+  if (downstream != Http::CodecType::HTTP1) {","+    config_helper.addConfigModifier(","+        [downstream](","+            envoy::extensions::filters::network::http_connection_manager::v3::HttpConnectionManager&","+                hcm) {","+          if (downstream == Http::CodecType::HTTP2) {","+            hcm.mutable_http2_protocol_options()->set_allow_connect(true);","+          } else {","+            hcm.mutable_http3_protocol_options()->set_allow_extended_connect(true);","+          }","+        });","+  }","+}","+"," INSTANTIATE_TEST_SUITE_P(","     Protocols, BodySizeLimitIntegrationTest,","     testing::ValuesIn(UpstreamDownstreamIntegrationTest::getDefaultTestParams()),","@@ -50,6 +81,22 @@ TEST_P(BodySizeLimitIntegrationTest, RouterRequestAndResponseWithZeroByteBodyBuf","   testRouterRequestAndResponseWithBody(0, 0, false);"," }"," ","+// A malformed HTTP/1 request gets its error reply through the filter before any request headers","+// exist, so the filter must not read them.","+TEST_P(BodySizeLimitIntegrationTest, MalformedHttp1RequestRejected) {","+  if (!testing_downstream_filter_ || downstreamProtocol() != Http::CodecType::HTTP1) {","+    return;","+  }","+  config_helper_.prependFilter(ConfigHelper::smallBodySizeLimitFilter(),","+                               testing_downstream_filter_);","+  initialize();","+","+  std::string response;","+  sendRawHttpAndWaitForResponse(","+      lookupPort(\"http\"), \"POST / HTTP/1.1\\r\\nHost: host\\r\\nbad header\\r\\n\\r\\n\", &response, false);","+  EXPECT_THAT(response, testing::StartsWith(\"HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request\\r\\n\"));","+}","+"," TEST_P(BodySizeLimitIntegrationTest, RouterRequestSizeLimitExceeded) {","   // Make sure the connection isn't closed during request upload.","   // Without a large drain-close it's possible that the local reply will be sent","@@ -117,6 +164,126 @@ TEST_P(BodySizeLimitIntegrationTest, RouterHeaderRequestSizeLimitExceeded) {","   cleanupUpstreamAndDownstream();"," }"," ","+// Test that bytes sent on an upgraded WebSocket connection are not counted toward the limit.","+TEST_P(BodySizeLimitIntegrationTest, WebSocketTrafficNotLimited) {","+  allowExtendedConnect(config_helper_, downstreamProtocol(), upstreamProtocol());","+  config_helper_.addConfigModifier(","+      [](envoy::extensions::filters::network::http_connection_manager::v3::HttpConnectionManager&","+             hcm) { hcm.add_upgrade_configs()->set_upgrade_type(\"websocket\"); });","+  config_helper_.prependFilter(ConfigHelper::smallBodySizeLimitFilter(),","+                               testing_downstream_filter_);","+  initialize();","+","+  codec_client_ = makeHttpConnection(lookupPort(\"http\"));","+  auto encoder_decoder = codec_client_->startRequest(","+      Http::TestRequestHeaderMapImpl{{\":method\", \"GET\"},","+                                     {\":path\", \"/websocket/test\"},","+                                     {\":scheme\", \"http\"},","+                                     {\":authority\", \"sni.lyft.com\"},","+                                     {\"upgrade\", \"websocket\"},","+                                     {\"connection\", \"keep-alive, upgrade\"}});","+  request_encoder_ = &encoder_decoder.first;","+  auto response = std::move(encoder_decoder.second);","+","+  ASSERT_TRUE(fake_upstreams_[0]->waitForHttpConnection(*dispatcher_, fake_upstream_connection_));","+  ASSERT_TRUE(fake_upstream_connection_->waitForNewStream(*dispatcher_, upstream_request_));","+  ASSERT_TRUE(upstream_request_->waitForHeadersComplete());","+  upstream_request_->encodeHeaders(Http::TestResponseHeaderMapImpl{{\":status\", \"101\"},","+                                                                   {\"connection\", \"upgrade\"},","+                                                                   {\"upgrade\", \"websocket\"}},","+                                   false);","+  response->waitForHeaders();","+  EXPECT_EQ(\"101\", response->headers().getStatusValue());","+","+  // Send more than the 1024 byte limit over the upgraded connection.","+  const std::string payload(4096, 'a');","+  codec_client_->sendData(*request_encoder_, payload, false);","+  ASSERT_TRUE(upstream_request_->waitForData(*dispatcher_, payload));","+  EXPECT_FALSE(response->complete());","+  // The filter's counters only exist under this name in the downstream filter chain.","+  if (testing_downstream_filter_) {","+    EXPECT_EQ(0,","+              test_server_->counter(\"http.config_test.body_size_limit.rq_body_too_large\")->value());","+  }","+","+  cleanupUpstreamAndDownstream();","+}","+","+// Test that upgrade headers alone don't lift the limit: bytes sent before the upstream accepts","+// the upgrade are still counted.","+TEST_P(BodySizeLimitIntegrationTest, UpgradeRequestBodyLimitedBeforeAccepted) {","+  if (!testing_downstream_filter_ || downstreamProtocol() != Http::CodecType::HTTP1 ||","+      upstreamProtocol() != Http::CodecType::HTTP1) {","+    return;","+  }","+  config_helper_.addConfigModifier(","+      [](envoy::extensions::filters::network::http_connection_manager::v3::HttpConnectionManager&","+             hcm) {","+        hcm.add_upgrade_configs()->set_upgrade_type(\"websocket\");","+        hcm.mutable_delayed_close_timeout()->set_seconds(2000 * 1000);","+      });","+  config_helper_.prependFilter(ConfigHelper::smallBodySizeLimitFilter(),","+                               testing_downstream_filter_);","+  initialize();","+","+  codec_client_ = makeHttpConnection(lookupPort(\"http\"));","+  auto encoder_decoder = codec_client_->startRequest(","+      Http::TestRequestHeaderMapImpl{{\":method\", \"POST\"},","+                                     {\":path\", \"/websocket/test\"},","+                                     {\":scheme\", \"http\"},","+                                     {\":authority\", \"sni.lyft.com\"},","+                                     {\"upgrade\", \"websocket\"},","+                                     {\"connection\", \"keep-alive, upgrade\"}});","+  request_encoder_ = &encoder_decoder.first;","+  auto response = std::move(encoder_decoder.second);","+  codec_client_->sendData(*request_encoder_, std::string(4096, 'a'), false);","+","+  ASSERT_TRUE(response->waitForEndStream());","+  EXPECT_EQ(\"413\", response->headers().getStatusValue());","+  test_server_->waitForCounter(\"http.config_test.body_size_limit.rq_body_too_large\",","+                               testing::Eq(1));","+  cleanupUpstreamAndDownstream();","+}","+","+// Test that bytes sent on an accepted CONNECT tunnel are not counted toward the limit.","+TEST_P(BodySizeLimitIntegrationTest, ConnectTunnelTrafficNotLimited) {","+  if (downstreamProtocol() == Http::CodecType::HTTP3) {","+    return;","+  }","+  config_helper_.addConfigModifier(","+      [](envoy::extensions::filters::network::http_connection_manager::v3::HttpConnectionManager&","+             hcm) { ConfigHelper::setConnectConfig(hcm, false, false); });","+  config_helper_.prependFilter(ConfigHelper::smallBodySizeLimitFilter(),","+                               testing_downstream_filter_);","+  initialize();","+","+  codec_client_ = makeHttpConnection(lookupPort(\"http\"));","+  auto encoder_decoder = codec_client_->startRequest(","+      Http::TestRequestHeaderMapImpl{{\":method\", \"CONNECT\"}, {\":authority\", \"foo.lyft.com:80\"}});","+  request_encoder_ = &encoder_decoder.first;","+  auto response = std::move(encoder_decoder.second);","+","+  ASSERT_TRUE(fake_upstreams_[0]->waitForHttpConnection(*dispatcher_, fake_upstream_connection_));","+  ASSERT_TRUE(fake_upstream_connection_->waitForNewStream(*dispatcher_, upstream_request_));","+  ASSERT_TRUE(upstream_request_->waitForHeadersComplete());","+  upstream_request_->encodeHeaders(default_response_headers_, false);","+  response->waitForHeaders();","+  EXPECT_EQ(\"200\", response->headers().getStatusValue());","+","+  // Send more than the 1024 byte limit over the tunnel.","+  const std::string payload(4096, 'a');","+  codec_client_->sendData(*request_encoder_, payload, false);","+  ASSERT_TRUE(upstream_request_->waitForData(*dispatcher_, payload));","+  EXPECT_FALSE(response->complete());","+  // The filter's counters only exist under this name in the downstream filter chain.","+  if (testing_downstream_filter_) {","+    EXPECT_EQ(0,","+              test_server_->counter(\"http.config_test.body_size_limit.rq_body_too_large\")->value());","+  }","+","+  cleanupUpstreamAndDownstream();","+}","+"," // Test that the filter can be disabled on a specific route using the generic"," // FilterConfig{disabled: true} mechanism in typed_per_filter_config."," TEST_P(BodySizeLimitIntegrationTest, RouteDisabled) {"],"additions":167,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"test/extensions/filters/http/body_size_limit/body_size_limit_filter_test.cc","lines":["@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@"," "," using testing::InSequence;"," using testing::NiceMock;","+using testing::Return;"," "," namespace Envoy {"," namespace Extensions {","@@ -34,6 +35,12 @@ class BodySizeLimitFilterTest : public testing::Test {","     filter_.setDecoderFilterCallbacks(callbacks_);","   }"," ","+  // Makes `headers` the request headers the filter reads back when the response arrives.","+  void setRequestHeaders(Http::RequestHeaderMap& headers) {","+    ON_CALL(callbacks_, requestHeaders())","+        .WillByDefault(Return(Http::RequestHeaderMapOptRef(headers)));","+  }","+","   Stats::TestUtil::TestStore store_;","   NiceMock<Http::MockStreamDecoderFilterCallbacks> callbacks_;","   BodySizeLimitFilterConfigSharedPtr config_;","@@ -117,6 +124,151 @@ TEST_F(BodySizeLimitFilterTest, DataTooLong) {","   EXPECT_EQ(1, counter(\"rq_body_too_large\"));"," }"," ","+TEST_F(BodySizeLimitFilterTest, UpgradeNotLimitedAfterAccepted) {","+  auto small_config = setupConfig(5);","+  BodySizeLimitFilter small_filter(small_config);","+  small_filter.setDecoderFilterCallbacks(callbacks_);","+","+  Http::TestRequestHeaderMapImpl headers{","+      {\":method\", \"GET\"}, {\"upgrade\", \"websocket\"}, {\"connection\", \"upgrade\"}};","+  setRequestHeaders(headers);","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue, small_filter.decodeHeaders(headers, false));","+  Http::TestResponseHeaderMapImpl response_headers{","+      {\":status\", \"101\"}, {\"upgrade\", \"websocket\"}, {\"connection\", \"upgrade\"}};","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue,","+            small_filter.encodeHeaders(response_headers, false));","+  Buffer::OwnedImpl data(\"Hello, world!\");","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterDataStatus::Continue, small_filter.decodeData(data, false));","+  EXPECT_EQ(0, counter(\"rq_body_too_large\"));","+}","+","+// A 101 without upgrade headers isn't treated as a tunnel by the connection manager either.","+TEST_F(BodySizeLimitFilterTest, UpgradeLimitedAfter101WithoutUpgradeHeaders) {","+  auto small_config = setupConfig(5);","+  BodySizeLimitFilter small_filter(small_config);","+  small_filter.setDecoderFilterCallbacks(callbacks_);","+","+  Http::TestRequestHeaderMapImpl headers{","+      {\":method\", \"POST\"}, {\"upgrade\", \"websocket\"}, {\"connection\", \"upgrade\"}};","+  setRequestHeaders(headers);","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue, small_filter.decodeHeaders(headers, false));","+  Http::TestResponseHeaderMapImpl response_headers{{\":status\", \"101\"}};","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue,","+            small_filter.encodeHeaders(response_headers, false));","+  Buffer::OwnedImpl data(\"Hello, world!\");","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterDataStatus::StopIterationNoBuffer, small_filter.decodeData(data, false));","+  EXPECT_EQ(1, counter(\"rq_body_too_large\"));","+}","+","+TEST_F(BodySizeLimitFilterTest, UpgradeLimitedWhenRefused) {","+  auto small_config = setupConfig(5);","+  BodySizeLimitFilter small_filter(small_config);","+  small_filter.setDecoderFilterCallbacks(callbacks_);","+  // A 200 without upgrade headers, from an upstream that refused the upgrade or from a local","+  // reply, doesn't open a tunnel.","+","+  Http::TestRequestHeaderMapImpl headers{","+      {\":method\", \"POST\"}, {\"upgrade\", \"websocket\"}, {\"connection\", \"upgrade\"}};","+  setRequestHeaders(headers);","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue, small_filter.decodeHeaders(headers, false));","+  Http::TestResponseHeaderMapImpl response_headers{{\":status\", \"200\"}};","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue,","+            small_filter.encodeHeaders(response_headers, false));","+  Buffer::OwnedImpl data(\"Hello, world!\");","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterDataStatus::StopIterationNoBuffer, small_filter.decodeData(data, false));","+  EXPECT_EQ(1, counter(\"rq_body_too_large\"));","+}","+","+// A failed handshake that keeps the upgrade headers is a tunnel to the connection manager, but","+// the upstream refused it, so the body stays limited.","+TEST_F(BodySizeLimitFilterTest, UpgradeLimitedAfter4xxWithUpgradeHeaders) {","+  auto small_config = setupConfig(5);","+  BodySizeLimitFilter small_filter(small_config);","+  small_filter.setDecoderFilterCallbacks(callbacks_);","+","+  Http::TestRequestHeaderMapImpl headers{","+      {\":method\", \"GET\"}, {\"upgrade\", \"websocket\"}, {\"connection\", \"upgrade\"}};","+  setRequestHeaders(headers);","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue, small_filter.decodeHeaders(headers, false));","+  Http::TestResponseHeaderMapImpl response_headers{","+      {\":status\", \"403\"}, {\"upgrade\", \"websocket\"}, {\"connection\", \"upgrade\"}};","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue,","+            small_filter.encodeHeaders(response_headers, false));","+  Buffer::OwnedImpl data(\"Hello, world!\");","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterDataStatus::StopIterationNoBuffer, small_filter.decodeData(data, false));","+  EXPECT_EQ(1, counter(\"rq_body_too_large\"));","+}","+","+TEST_F(BodySizeLimitFilterTest, PlainRequestStillLimitedAfterResponse) {","+  auto small_config = setupConfig(5);","+  BodySizeLimitFilter small_filter(small_config);","+  small_filter.setDecoderFilterCallbacks(callbacks_);","+","+  Http::TestRequestHeaderMapImpl headers{{\":method\", \"POST\"}};","+  setRequestHeaders(headers);","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue, small_filter.decodeHeaders(headers, false));","+  Http::TestResponseHeaderMapImpl response_headers{{\":status\", \"200\"}};","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue,","+            small_filter.encodeHeaders(response_headers, false));","+  Buffer::OwnedImpl data(\"Hello, world!\");","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterDataStatus::StopIterationNoBuffer, small_filter.decodeData(data, false));","+  EXPECT_EQ(1, counter(\"rq_body_too_large\"));","+}","+","+TEST_F(BodySizeLimitFilterTest, ConnectNotLimitedAfterAccepted) {","+  auto small_config = setupConfig(5);","+  BodySizeLimitFilter small_filter(small_config);","+  small_filter.setDecoderFilterCallbacks(callbacks_);","+","+  Http::TestRequestHeaderMapImpl headers{{\":method\", \"CONNECT\"}, {\":authority\", \"host:443\"}};","+  setRequestHeaders(headers);","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue, small_filter.decodeHeaders(headers, false));","+  Http::TestResponseHeaderMapImpl response_headers{{\":status\", \"200\"}};","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue,","+            small_filter.encodeHeaders(response_headers, false));","+  Buffer::OwnedImpl data(\"Hello, world!\");","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterDataStatus::Continue, small_filter.decodeData(data, false));","+  EXPECT_EQ(0, counter(\"rq_body_too_large\"));","+}","+","+TEST_F(BodySizeLimitFilterTest, ConnectLimitedWhenRefused) {","+  auto small_config = setupConfig(5);","+  BodySizeLimitFilter small_filter(small_config);","+  small_filter.setDecoderFilterCallbacks(callbacks_);","+","+  Http::TestRequestHeaderMapImpl headers{{\":method\", \"CONNECT\"}, {\":authority\", \"host:443\"}};","+  setRequestHeaders(headers);","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue, small_filter.decodeHeaders(headers, false));","+  Http::TestResponseHeaderMapImpl response_headers{{\":status\", \"403\"}};","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue,","+            small_filter.encodeHeaders(response_headers, false));","+  Buffer::OwnedImpl data(\"Hello, world!\");","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterDataStatus::StopIterationNoBuffer, small_filter.decodeData(data, false));","+  EXPECT_EQ(1, counter(\"rq_body_too_large\"));","+}","+","+// A later filter that strips the upgrade headers makes the router forward a plain request, so even","+// an upgrade response must not lift the limit.","+TEST_F(BodySizeLimitFilterTest, UpgradeLimitedWhenLaterFilterStripsUpgrade) {","+  auto small_config = setupConfig(5);","+  BodySizeLimitFilter small_filter(small_config);","+  small_filter.setDecoderFilterCallbacks(callbacks_);","+","+  Http::TestRequestHeaderMapImpl headers{","+      {\":method\", \"POST\"}, {\"upgrade\", \"websocket\"}, {\"connection\", \"upgrade\"}};","+  setRequestHeaders(headers);","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue, small_filter.decodeHeaders(headers, false));","+  headers.removeUpgrade();","+  headers.removeConnection();","+  Http::TestResponseHeaderMapImpl response_headers{","+      {\":status\", \"101\"}, {\"upgrade\", \"websocket\"}, {\"connection\", \"upgrade\"}};","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue,","+            small_filter.encodeHeaders(response_headers, false));","+  Buffer::OwnedImpl data(\"Hello, world!\");","+  EXPECT_EQ(Http::FilterDataStatus::StopIterationNoBuffer, small_filter.decodeData(data, false));","+  EXPECT_EQ(1, counter(\"rq_body_too_large\"));","+}","+"," TEST_F(BodySizeLimitFilterTest, Unlimited) {","   auto zero_config = setupConfig(0);","   BodySizeLimitFilter zero_filter(zero_config);"],"additions":152,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"test/extensions/filters/http/body_size_limit/config_test.cc","lines":["@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ TEST(BodySizeLimitFilterFactoryTest, Body